# Plan structure graph layout (anti-regression)

## Binding

ADR-0043 V6 §6: **Structure layout is top→bottom** (parallel siblings side-by-side).

## Forbidden

- Forcing `direction: 'lr'` (or any left→right) on `PlanDagGraph` `mode="structure"` to “fill a wide rail.”
- That regression shipped in commit `565ba71` and collapsed sequential payroll-style plans into **one horizontal card strip** with truncated labels and a huge empty vertical gutter.

## Required

- `STRUCTURE_LAYOUT_OPTIONS.direction === 'tb'` in `PlanDagGraph.jsx`.
- Letterboxing / unreadably small nodes → fix **fitMode / pan / nodeW·nodeH**, not direction.
- Structure `fitMode` must be **`none`** + **`contentSized`** (never stretch a short DAG into a tall rail — that blew cards to ~2×). Cap fitZoomCeil ≤ 1 when auto-fitting.
- Long-span Sugiyama dummies must stay on visible lanes / neighbor channels — never park at raw group index (far-right edge loops).
- Keep Vitest: `structure mode: ADR-0043 — top→bottom, never LR strip`.

## Do not introduce

New DAG libraries (dagre/elk/React Flow) — ADR-0011 / 0012.
